google/dawn @ 6c1e27710cd1 (main, 2026-09-26): zero the mapped-range shadow in
emwgpuBufferGetMappedRange.

Proposal only. picovoxel, an unofficial community TypeScript/WebAssembly binding
of LEAP 71's PicoGK, found this while evaluating emdawnwebgpu for WebGPU
compute experiments (scripts/build-emdawnwebgpu-spike.sh). Dawn takes changes
through Gerrit and the Chromium issue tracker; this diff is the one-line change
such a CL would carry.

The defect (third_party/emdawnwebgpu/pkg/webgpu/src/library_webgpu.js:1063).
The shadow buffer comes from _memalign and is zeroed with
HEAPU8.fill(0, data, mapped.byteLength). TypedArray.fill takes an end index,
not a length, and data is a heap address normally far above
mapped.byteLength, so the call fills nothing. On unmap the whole shadow is
copied into the mapped range, so bytes the application did not write reach the
GPU buffer as leftover heap contents.

The fix: pass data + mapped.byteLength as the end index.

Output values: bytes the application writes are unchanged; bytes it does not
write become zero instead of leftover heap contents.

Not reproduced in a browser; derived from reading the source at the commit
above.

Applies with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0` at the root of a Dawn checkout.
Not applied by picovoxel's build; see upstream/README.md.

--- a/third_party/emdawnwebgpu/pkg/webgpu/src/library_webgpu.js
+++ b/third_party/emdawnwebgpu/pkg/webgpu/src/library_webgpu.js
@@ -1060,7 +1060,7 @@
     }
 
     var data = _memalign(16, mapped.byteLength);
-    HEAPU8.fill(0, data, mapped.byteLength);
+    HEAPU8.fill(0, data, data + mapped.byteLength);
     WebGPU.Internals.bufferOnUnmaps[bufferPtr].push(() => {
       new Uint8Array(mapped).set(HEAPU8.subarray(data, data + mapped.byteLength));
       _free(data);
